Z||000000||mdjoneses||11-25-2000||11:34 AM||||Has anyone had their manual tranny go bad? If so what kind of noise and trouble did it cause? Any warning signs? I think mine is shot. Thanx  Mark||||reg||9
Z||000001||terryk||11-25-2000||02:14 PM||||I usually starts with hard shifting although that can be caused by bad cable adjustments. Bearing noise is next (grinding, whinning, screeching), then no gear at all.<P>The 4spds are pretty good trans so I'd check the cable adjustments and clutch first.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mdjoneses||11-25-2000||05:46 PM||||That's good news. My 86se2.8/4speed was making noise for a long time. If I let off the gas while it was in gear it made some noise. Then yesterday it started making noise even when I gave it gas. Now it's grinding when I put it in gear. Kinda like when your having trouble finding reverse. I'll check the Pontiac Service Manual for symptons like mine.   Thanx    Mark||||reg||2
Z||000003||penetrator||06-10-2001||04:24 PM||||This sounds just like mine 4speed. When it stars to make the noise it is only noising on the 1st, 2nd and 3rd gear, not the 4th gear. And some times the sound comes when i have no gear in (Neutral) and the foot off the clutch, but the noise is not screetching, just crunching, and it sounds when i accelerate as well, but in higher speed it disapears. And it makes me crazy. It shifts just fine(except the reverse gear can make some noise when i put it in) , and it accelerates just fine as well. <P>And i got the advice to drive til it breaks down and then u see whats was wrong. =(<BR>||||reg||10
